A||||8||Jncomutt||MSD Coil Problem||||1||
Z||000000||Jncomutt||07-11-2001||03:54 PM||||Just picked up a Blaster GM Coil.  I noticed it would plug directly to my 86 2.5.  When I actually took it out of the package and went to connect it to my 84 2.5, the plug is totally different.  Can I just cut off the connectors and spice on the other????  Or do they sell an adapter harness??  Or, am I screwed for the $55 I paid for this thing???||||reg||1
Z||000001||DecadenceR||07-11-2001||05:55 PM||||You can just cut & splice the wires. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Neal||07-11-2001||07:33 PM||||I have the MSD blaster coil and it just plugs right in.  Its a 6cyl though...  I thought the 4cyl used the same plugs.  is it possible you got the wrong coil?||||reg||1
Z||000003||DecadenceR||07-11-2001||08:03 PM||||The 84 was a totally different connector. I made that mistake when I got my Accel coil. They changed it for 85 and up. The 6 is slightly different from the 4cyl too. I tried using the wires from the 6 so i could use the coil on my 4, and it's no dice...||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jncomutt||07-11-2001||10:51 PM||||So Decad...   1 post says it'll work, the other no... should I just try it???||||reg||1
Z||000005||DecadenceR||07-11-2001||11:36 PM||||If you take the wires from a 4-cyl, it'll work. If you take it from a 6-cyl, it won't work. Go for it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jncomutt||07-12-2001||02:07 AM||||Ahh.. I see now... Gotcha, thanx for the help, as always!!||||reg||1
Z||000007||fotofrank||07-12-2001||01:27 PM||||I used the coil connectors from an '85 duke on my '84 duke. Spliced them in and it works well. I also have an MSD 6A and only 2 of the wires from the coil are used if that. The tach plugs into the MSD unit. Good luck with the splice.<P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://www.homestead.com/fotofrank/foto1.html||||reg||10
Z||000008||Jncomutt||07-12-2001||07:59 PM||||Splice Worked Great!||||reg||1
